WHY THIS LICENSE EXISTS
-----------------------

This software runs security-critical infrastructure. Its entire value rests on a
promise: that the system does exactly what it says it does, and nothing else. A
promise like that is worthless if you have to take our word for it. So we are
giving you the means to check.

You may read every line of this source code. You may build it yourself. You may
run it to confirm it behaves as described, and you may reproduce our results
independently. If our claims are true, you can verify that they are true — from
the source, without asking us, without trusting us. That transparency is the
point, and it is why this code is open for you to inspect.

This is not open-source software, and we are honest about the one thing we hold
back: our patents. We invented the methods this software embodies, and we keep
the patent rights to them. We use those rights defensively — to stop this work
from being copied, forked, or reimplemented into a competing product. You are
free to look, learn, build, and verify. You are not free to take the patented
inventions and run them in production or ship them in a competing system without
a separate license from us.

That is the whole bargain, in one sentence: a fully transparent, independently
verifiable codebase, with the patents reserved so it cannot be turned into a
competitor. Inspect and verify all you like. Practicing the patented inventions
takes our permission.

The formal terms follow. Where the plain-language explanation above and the
formal terms below differ, the formal terms govern.


